oracle GNU Make 4.4.1
outcome success
file Makefile kept 8
| # The write changed a directory, and GNU Make counts it as a command for that
| # reason and no other — `++command_count` in `func_file`, with a comment
| # saying so. A `$(wildcard)` further down the same recipe therefore looks
| # again, and finds what the line above it wrote.
| all:
| 	@printf 'before [%s]\n' '$(wildcard *.written)' > out
| 	$(file > made.written,contents)
| 	@printf 'after [%s]\n' '$(wildcard *.written)' >> out
file made.written touched 1
| contents
file out touched 2
| before []
| after [made.written]
